  "metadata": {
    "title": "Root tissue segmentation dataset",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.5841376",
    "publication_date": "2022-01-12",
    "description": "<p>The PHDFM dataset is composed of fluorescence microscopy images of root tissue samples from <em>A. thaliana</em>, using the ratiometric fluorescent indicator 8\u2010hydroxypyrene\u20101,3,6\u2010trisulfonic acid trisodium salt (HPTS). This semantic segmentation training dataset consists of 2D microscopy images (the brightfield channel for excitation at 405 nm), each containing a segmentation mask as an additional image channel (manually annotated by plant biologists). The segmentation masks classify pixels into the following 5 labels with the corresponding IDs: background (0), root tissue (1), early elongation zone (2), late elongation zone (3), and meristematic zone (4).</p>",
